{
  "_comment": [
    "Approximate centroid coordinates (WGS84) for every Hong Kong subdistrict",
    "that appears in the source data, plus a district-level fallback.",
    "",
    "Coordinates rather than a precomputed N-by-N distance matrix: 106 points is",
    "a 4KB file where the matrix is 11,236 entries, and a new subdistrict costs",
    "one line instead of a rebuild. Distance is computed by haversine at runtime,",
    "which is microseconds and needs no network call — the pipeline must never",
    "depend on a maps API, both for air-gapped operation and because a detector",
    "whose answer depends on an external service is not reproducible for audit.",
    "",
    "These are centroids, so the distance between two points UNDERSTATES the",
    "true travel distance (it ignores terrain, harbour crossings and road",
    "routing) and reads as zero within a single subdistrict. That bias is",
    "deliberate: it makes the implied velocity a LOWER bound, so the geo-velocity",
    "rule under-flags rather than over-flags. See docs Detection_Flow_Diagrams.md",
    "section 5.4."
  ],
